      "title": "Appendix",
      "html": "<img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m4-015-appendix-1.png\" alt=\"Appendix – Details of outstanding matters relating to share-based payments\n\nShare options\n\nOn 1 October 20X5, the five executive directors were each granted 15,000 share options which could\nbe exercised on 30 September 20X8 if the directors remained with the company until this date. Each\noption entitled the director to one £0.50 share. The exercise price depended on the average growth rate\nof new customers over the 3-year period:\n\n                           Exercise price at 30  Fair value at 1 October         Fair value at 30\nGrowth rate                 September 20X8                20X5       September 20X8\n                                        £/option                £/option                £/option\nUp to/equal to 8%                         35.00                    9.00                  12.00\nOver 8%                                 25.00                  15.00                  21.00\n\nIn each of the 2 years from 1 October 20X5, the annual growth rate of new customers was 9%. In the\nyear ended 30 September 20X8, the growth rate was 5%.\n\nOne of the directors retired on 31 March 20X8. The remaining four directors were still employed at 30\nSeptember 20X8 and three of these directors exercised all of their share options. Cash received was\nrecognised as Dr Cash and cash equivalents and Cr SPL – other operating income. The remaining\ndirector chose not to exercise the options and they lapsed. The market value per share on 30\nSeptember 20X8 was £38.\n\nVictory has recognised the value of these share options as Dr SPL – staff costs and Cr Retained\nearnings. The balance on this reserve at 30 September 20X7 was £750,000. No other accounting has\ntaken place.\n\nShare appreciation rights\n\nOn 1 October 20X6, Victory granted 50 share appreciation rights (SAR) to each of its 1,420 employees\non the condition that the employees remain with the company for the next 3 years until 30 September\n20X9. Payment will be made on 31 October 20X9. The scheme was correctly accounted for in the\nfinancial statements for the year ended 30 September 20X7.\n\nYou have obtained the following information to allow you to post the necessary journal entries for the\nyear ended 30 September 20X8:\n\nYear ended 30            Employees that left     Further employees         Fair value at 30\nSeptember                        during year      expected to leave    September (£/SAR)\n\n20X7                                   96                  200                    3.50\n20X8                                   115                  100                    3.80\n\n\n\n16\">"
