      "title": "Appendix",
      "html": "<img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m4-016-appendix-1.png\" alt=\"Appendix – Relevant information relating to share-based payment matters\n\nThe board of directors decided to introduce a new scheme for managers from 1 June 20X3 onwards.\n\nManagers’ incentive scheme\n\nThe scheme started on 1 June 20X3 and applies to all 160 of the management staff employed at that\ndate. The scheme offers share appreciation rights on a notional 4,000 ordinary shares to each manager\nprovided they stay with the company until 31 May 20X7. No managers may join the scheme after 1\nJune 20X3.\n\nOver the term of the scheme, it is estimated that eight mangers will leave the company each year and\nthat six will join annually. It is estimated that the fair value of a share appreciation right at 31 May 20X4\nwill be £3.60.\n\nSorrento pays tax at 20%.\n\nNew retail outlets\n\nSorrento is considering the acquisition of several new retail outlets during the year ending 31 May 20X4.\nThe outlets have a combined asking price of £23m. The directors of Sorrento are considering two\nalternative bids for the outlets:\n\na) A cash bid of £23m, or\nb) An issue to the seller of four million £0.50 ordinary shares in Sorrento. At the date of issue of the\n    shares to the seller, it is estimated that each share would have a fair value of £6.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                               17\">"
